  "prefLabel": "Dec 201.04 Waiver of Rules",
  "priorExpiration": "2001-03-17",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Dec 201.04 Waiver of Rules.\n\n(a) Upon its own motion, or upon written request, the committee shall waive the provisions of any rule, except where precluded by statute, provided that:\n\n(1) Such waiver will enable the committee to either expedite the proceeding or complete the proceeding in a more orderly manner;\n\n(2) Compliance with the rule would be onerous or inapplicable given the circumstances of the affected person; or\n\n(3) A specifically defined alternative procedure is proposed which shall result in a substantially equivalent result consistent with the principles embodied in said rule.\n\nSource. #4235, eff 2-20-87, EXPIRED: 2-20-93\n\nNew. #5700, INTERIM, eff 9-17-93, EXPIRED: 1-15-94\n\nNew. #5824, eff 8-30-94, EXPIRED: 8-30-00\n\nNew. #7366, INTERIM, eff 9-18-00, EXPIRED: 3-17-01\n\nNew. #9144-A, eff 4-24-08",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/dec100-200.html"
